+# Boost: site blog entries link in the user profile
+
+## Summary
+
+When blogs are enabled, the Miscellaneous section of a user profile now offers two blog links, so site-wide blog entries are reachable in Boost without the Navigation block.
+
+## User-visible changes
+
+- The existing profile link is renamed from "Blog entries" to **View my blog entries**. It opens the viewed user's own blog entries (for your own profile) as before.
+- A new link, **View site blog entries**, opens the site-wide blog listing at `/blog/index.php`.
+- Both links appear in the same places where the existing profile blog link was shown. For another user's profile, the personal link keeps its existing label ("View all blog entries").
+- When blogs are disabled, or the user cannot see blogs (for example, guests), neither link is shown.
+
+## Not changed
+
+- Personal and site-wide blog pages, their access controls, and blog capabilities are unchanged.
+- The Classic Navigation block is not reintroduced in Boost.
